			<div class="content" id="post-content-4842068">
									

<p>While I can see the merits of a funny article and or tale about klavigar saarn being fed up with modern sarkicism, this fails to make it work.</p>
<p>The article (minus interview) could be pretty much summed up as &quot;this is the apartment of klavigar saarn from sarkicism. That one.&quot; In fact, you could probably replace the article entirely with those words and you wouldn't lose any narrative cohesiveness.</p>
<p>As for the interview, I don't really have much negative things to say about it. It's a bit odd that Saarn is talking like someone from the 21st century, but that's not really much of an issue. Unfortunately, I don't really have anything good to say either. Didn't really find it funny or otherwise appealing.</p>
<p>If the description portion of the article was better , maybe I could be convinced to novote this. But with the current state of it, it's a -1.</p>

